{"name":"Dead Sea","hex":"#77eeee","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Dead Sea","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A lake in the Middle East in Palestine and Jordan, noted for high salinity and for its banks being the lowest land-based elevation on Earth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Dead_Sea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dead Sea","blocks":[{"text":"The Dead Sea, also known by other names, is a landlocked salt lake bordered by Jordan to the east, the West Bank to the west and Israel to the southwest. It lies in the endorheic basin of the Jordan Rift Valley, and its main tributary is the Jordan River."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Dead_Sea_beach_00.JPG/330px-Dead_Sea_beach_00.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dead_Sea","wikidata":"Q23883"},{"title":"Dead Sea (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Dead Sea is a 2024 American crime horror film written and directed by Phil Volken. It stars Dean Cameron, Isabel Gravitt, Koa Tom, Garrett Wareing, Alexander Wraith and Genneya Walton. The film is about a young woman and her two friends that are rescued by a fishing vessel's captain, unaware that the ship harbors a chilling secret."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/00/Dead_sea_movie.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dead_Sea_(film)","wikidata":"Q127869960"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Dead_Sea_beach_00.JPG/500px-Dead_Sea_beach_00.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Dead_Sea_beach_00.JPG/1280px-Dead_Sea_beach_00.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Dead_Sea_beach_00.JPG/500px-Dead_Sea_beach_00.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADead_Sea_beach_00.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Dead_Sea_Galilee.jpg/500px-Dead_Sea_Galilee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Dead_Sea_Galilee.jpg/500px-Dead_Sea_Galilee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Satellite photograph, showing the location of the Dead Sea east of the Mediterranean Sea","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADead_Sea_Galilee.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Dead_Sea%2C_Jordanian_Shore.jpg/500px-Dead_Sea%2C_Jordanian_Shore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Dead_Sea%2C_Jordanian_Shore.jpg/1280px-Dead_Sea%2C_Jordanian_Shore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Dead_Sea%2C_Jordanian_Shore.jpg/500px-Dead_Sea%2C_Jordanian_Shore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Jordanian shore of the Dead